{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations","id":1385888,"title":"I don't really understand the path of evil revelations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-05T11:57:54-07:00","id":1385888,"title":"I don't really understand the path of evil revelations","content":"The tenents of the path seems to be all about serving the demons,doing whatever the demons want. It's basically slavery isnt it? The path doesn't mention what the infernalist gains in the whole deal. I completely understand why a vampire would deals in demons fpr money,power ir artifacts<br /> But why would anyone sell their soul if there isn't anything but slavery to receive in return?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-05-2020, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T12:09:37-07:00","id":1385890,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've never understood that path, either. Infernalists should just have low ratings in humanity or other paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T12:29:19-07:00","id":1385894,"title":"","content":"It's just a way to allow Infernalist vampires to function without a constant risk of Wassail, or centuries-long periods of torpor. The worst aspect of the Paths really, be as horrible as you want with practically none of the downsides of low Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T12:41:02-07:00","id":1385899,"title":"","content":"But why do they sell their souls? What are the denons offering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:05:14-07:00","id":1385905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1385899#post1385899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why do they sell their souls? What are the denons offering?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine that it's different for each infernalist. Power, greed, lust, really any of the Seven Deadly Sins are a good stepping off point for this. I don't think a concrete rule works for something like this because temptation is such an individual matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:12:24-07:00","id":1385909,"title":"","content":"Got it,thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:22:11-07:00","id":1385913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations#post1385888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tenents of the path seems to be all about serving the demons,doing whatever the demons want. It's basically slavery isnt it? The path doesn't mention what the infernalist gains in the whole deal. I completely understand why a vampire would deals in demons fpr money,power ir artifacts<br /> But why would anyone sell their soul if there isn't anything but slavery to receive in return?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Path of Evil Revelations basically is a trade-off of a vampire giving up his freedom for the security of a demon's protection. Many religions are based around the idea of submitting to a higher power and in the case of this one, the demon provides you material as well as spiritual benefits for indulging your worst appetites. If I were evangelizing the POER, I'd probably say that they would consider their &quot;slavery&quot; to be far superior to the Sabbat's freedom as they are free from the Vinculum and have patrons far stronger than mere mortals to protect them from the Antediluvians. They also may reject the idea that freedom as a concept actually exists since not all scientists or worldviews believe free will exists.<br /> <br /> At the lower levels of infernalism, the Path of Evil Revelations is not really any different than transactional religion. You trade your soul and the soul of your fellow converts for things like nice cars, wealths, points of Disciplines, and so on.<br /> <br /> At higher levels of infernalism, you willingly have embraced your Damnation and find the whole concept that owning your own soul ridiculous. After all, as a vampire you were always going to hell anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-05-2020, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:42:27-07:00","id":1385920,"title":"","content":"As to what they gain, by slicing off portions of your soul, you can gain &quot;Demonic Investments&quot; that grant various special abilities. Some of these are quite ridiculous. There's also &quot;Dark Thaumaturgy&quot;, which is just sorcery but EEEEVIILLLL!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:44:02-07:00","id":1385921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1385920#post1385920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to what they gain, by slicing off portions of your soul, you can gain &quot;Demonic Investments&quot; that grant various special abilities. Some of these are quite ridiculous. There's also &quot;Dark Thaumaturgy&quot;, which is just sorcery but EEEEVIILLLL!</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it's a pretty sweet deal.<br /> <br /> What are you doing with your soul after all? You're a vampire. You're already damned!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:48:43-07:00","id":1385923,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was always something that bothered me. Why would a demon even want the soul of a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:51:42-07:00","id":1385924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1385921#post1385921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, it's a pretty sweet deal.<br /> <br /> What are you doing with your soul after all? You're a vampire. You're already damned!</div> </div> </div> </div>One could interpret God's curse on Caine as not eternal punishment,but as a hardship imposed to teach Caine humility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:51:46-07:00","id":1385925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1385923#post1385923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that was always something that bothered me. Why would a demon even want the soul of a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're the demon equivalent of fast food. Quick and easy to buy.<br /> <br /> Really, vampires are more useful as a easy minion versus the value of their souls too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:14:43-07:00","id":1385936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1385924#post1385924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One could interpret God's curse on Caine as not eternal punishment,but as a hardship imposed to teach Caine humility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ding! Ding! Ding! Winner,winner....Chicken dinner........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:31:19-07:00","id":1385939,"title":"","content":"There is a flip side to the Path of Evil Revelations that you don't see if you are only looking at the Path. The demons are offering things of tangible value to the vampire.<ul><li>They will have access to low level demons who can act as spies and scouts.</li> <li>They will be able to select additional powers in the form of Demonic Investments.</li> <li>They will now have access to paths and rituals of Dark Thaumaturgy.</li> <li>They now have access to additional lore, secrets, and information that the demon can teach them. That could be the location of torpored vampires of potent blood, magical devices, or anything else that should be lost to history yet useful if found.</li> <li>If the vampire is close to surrendering to the Beast, they may even decide that adoption of the path is a way to prevent them from losing control at the last moment.</li> </ul>So there is an exchange of power in return for adoption of the path. I would say that no one willingly adopts the Path of Evil Revelation. You get conned into it thinking you're going to get all this power as you slowly get brainwashed into following a cult and surrendering your soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-05-2020, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:40:23-07:00","id":1385943,"title":"","content":"That makes more sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:47:09-07:00","id":1385944,"title":"","content":"Basically, the Path of Evil Revelations is what the Baali followed before later editions changed them to be semi-playable instead of infernalist villains akin to the Nephandi of Mage. It was meant to be utterly inhuman; replacing both Conscience and Self-Control with Conviction and Instinct.<br /> <br /> As I understand it, the root of the Path begins with the notion that the Vampire, by its nature, is Damned. In this it superficially resembles the Path of Cathari.<br /> <br /> But where the Cathari path teaches that their gnostic role is to keep mortals trapped in the material world by leading them to sin, the Path of Evil Revelations teaches that it is instead their duty as one of the Damned to aid the demons in tearing down Creation so that all can know the peace of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> In a real sense, their method of dealing with the Beast is to embrace what the Beast drives them to do and convince themselves that there is a higher purpose to what it demands of them (i.e. that their actions serve the higher purpose of a demon who will reward them when Hell comes to Earth)<br /> <br /> And if you don\u2019t think that level of self-deception is possible... just look at the Nazis who told themselves they weren\u2019t monsters because they were \u201cjust following orders\u201d and those ordered were justified and necessary. They didn\u2019t even have a ravening Beast actually inside them demanding atrocities as they herded millions into the gas chambers and ovens... just the urgings of other mortal men of higher rank.<br /> <br /> All that said, to my knowledge, there is only ONE canon vampire even on the Path of Evil Revelations; Shaitan (see The Chaos Factor), first to swear fealty to Baal and described as effectively \u201ca demon in a vampire\u2019s body)... and this was before all the retcons to the Baali that came in later editions.*<br /> <br /> As such, you could just as easily declare the Path to be defunct in the Modern Nights (save the actual Baali founder or founders) as even the Baali have abandoned it for the Path of the Hive.<br /> <br /> * I generally synchretize the conflicting accounts by saying that the Ashur who embraced Nergal, Moloch and the Nameless was actually Shaitan of the Chaos Factor.<br /> <br /> The three went on to found what most think of as the Baali Bloodline (they diablerized their way up to 4th at some point which is where the confusion comes in) that follows the Path of the Hive and believes that by causing atrocities they\u2019re keeping the demons asleep.<br /> <br /> Shaitan and the True Baali (the twelve oldest from before the Second City fell) who follow the Path of Evil Revelations are more than happy with this arrangement as it distracts their enemies with a false target who\u2019s actions they believe soothe the demons actually strengthen them and bring them closer to waking with each atrocity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T15:57:15-07:00","id":1385959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1385944#post1385944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that said, to my knowledge, there is only ONE canon vampire even on the Path of Evil Revelations; Shaitan (see The Chaos Factor), first to swear fealty to Baal and described as effectively \u201ca demon in a vampire\u2019s body)... and this was before all the retcons to the Baali that came in later editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Montreal By Night has several vampires on the Path of Evil Revelations, and I believe the Path was first described in the Player's Guide to the Sabbat first edition. The Path is something I associate far more with Sabbat Infernalists than I do with the Baali. Of course, I think the Baali has changed substantially from what I think they were originally supposed to be from what they are now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T16:19:22-07:00","id":1385963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1385923#post1385923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that was always something that bothered me. Why would a demon even want the soul of a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There's a reason why Infernalism is more common in the Sabbat than the Camarilla. Afterall its only a matter of time before your average cammy or Anarch goes to hell.. but the sabbat they have a system that keeps souls in!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T17:08:37-07:00","id":1385975,"title":"","content":"Every vampire loses their free will to some extant.<br /> <br /> The Beast has such a pervasive influence, especially as Humanity drops, that it must be terrifying to think one might become a slavering, primitive wight, barely capable of speech let alone free will. It looks a little like how in zombie movies there's always that one character who begs the others to &quot;not let me become one of those things.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Path of Evil Revelations promises not just temporal rewards (Investments, Dark Thaumaturgy, etc.), but also a means to easily avoid entering Wassail. Sure, there are other paths that don't involve slavery, but those are really hard. I mean, like getting a degree in philosophy hard. They take time, effort, study, and self-knowledge. It doesn't always work, even after all that effort.<br /> <br /> If you can find a demon, though, you just do what they tell you to do. All the time. Everytime. Usually they don't even ask anything too hard. After all, you're doing their bidding, so they'd rather if you succeed.<br /> <br /> Finally. Finally! You can relax, kick back, and let somebody else worry about all the messy moral quandries. Imagine what a relief this must be for a vampire who has been white-knuckling their control of the Beast for the past decade or century or so.<br /> <br /> Oh, somewhere down the line there'll be hell to pay... literally... but that should be centuries from now. Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T17:32:37-07:00","id":1385978,"title":"","content":"I think it's also the fact demons generally are, &quot;The Path of What I Want To Do Anyway&quot;<br /> <br /> It's just what they want you to do is be an evil hedonistic asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T17:51:55-07:00","id":1385981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations#post1385888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why would anyone sell their soul if there isn't anything but slavery to receive in return?</div> </div> </div> </div>being on the path of revelations doesn't mean you sold your soul,<br /> it just means you pledged yourself to the Infernal,<br /> hell, you don't even need investments to be on the path<br /> <br /> the path is about putting your faith in the Infernal to fight off the beast,<br /> <br /> In the sabbat, the path of revelations became popular due to the difficult lifestyle in the sabbat,<br /> the path of revelations (and infernalism in general) was a convenient way to stay sane without having to take on the hard roads (other paths)<br /> <br /> also, you don't need to be on the path of revelations to be infernalist<br /> <br /> if you check the origins of the path (path of screams), you'll notice that it has distinct differences to revelations,<br /> revelations feels more like a desperate path, or a damned path,<br /> while screams feels more ambitious (or at least, less desperate),<br /> it's a pattern common to sabbat paths","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T21:15:53-07:00","id":1385995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1385923#post1385923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that was always something that bothered me. Why would a demon even want the soul of a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly (to me), Demon: The Fallen has rules for vampires who become demons' thralls. Vampires don't naturally generate the Faith resource, the way mortals do, but they draw some from every mortal that they feed on. They have no way of noticing or processing the stuff themselves, being spiritually dead, but a demon can extract it from them as part of their bargain. <br /> <br /> D:tF offers some handy suggestions as to what a demon might be able to offer its thralls in return - mostly stat increases or minor supernatural powers, the kind of thing that a wiser vampire could cultivate on their own with experience and time. Wise people don't sell their souls.<br /> <br /> What the demon gets out of the deal is an already more powerful and resourceful than average thrall. The vampire can be as reliable a source of Faith as any mortal, because the vampire is going to have to feed anyway.<br /> <br /> Since the demon is taking something that the vampire gets while feeding, a Storyteller could easily rule that rising at sunset requires at least one or two extra blood point every day, and more if the demon needs to draw extra power from its followers in an emergency. The demon takes its due.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-06-2020, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T21:26:34-07:00","id":1385996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1385995#post1385995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interestingly (to me), Demon: The Fallen has rules for vampires who become demons' thralls. Vampires don't naturally generate the Faith resource, the way mortals do, but they draw some from every mortal that they feed on. They have no way of noticing or processing the stuff themselves, being spiritually dead, but a demon can extract it from them as part of their bargain.<br /> <br /> D:tF offers some handy suggestions as to what a demon might be able to offer its thralls in return - mostly stat increases or minor supernatural powers, the kind of thing that a wiser vampire could cultivate on their own with experience and time. Wise people don't sell their souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Underworld Unleashed, the Joker sold his soul for a box of cigars. Personally, I think he got a deal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T22:24:47-07:00","id":1386008,"title":"","content":"I'm sure that I've seen some block of text in a WoD book pointing out there's a difference between someone who's almost certain to go to Hell in general and someone whose soul is pledged as the property of a specific demon. Only the latter benefits said specific demon directly, so they have good reasons for striking up bargains; it's the person pledging their soul who will ultimately be no better off than they would have been otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T22:38:58-07:00","id":1386010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations#post1385888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tenents of the path seems to be all about serving the demons,doing whatever the demons want. It's basically slavery isnt it? The path doesn't mention what the infernalist gains in the whole deal. I completely understand why a vampire would deals in demons fpr money,power ir artifacts<br /> But why would anyone sell their soul if there isn't anything but slavery to receive in return?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of it is for those who have a mental breakdown over becoming a vampire and lose their purpose, but then find purpose and a bulwark against mindless Beasthood by embracing a place in the Hierarchy of Hell. And various wicked spirits encouraged this because hey free slaves!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T01:05:12-07:00","id":1386021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1385923#post1385923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that was always something that bothered me. Why would a demon even want the soul of a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda reminds me of the Chick tracts I keep finding; the Devil depicted therein <i>is a chump</i>.<br /> <br /> He offers money, influence, or even amazing magic powers to people who were <i>already</i> going to Hell, follows through on <i>his</i> end of the bargain, but once they go running to Jeebus crying, \u201cSave me, save me!\u201d, <i>he has no recourse</i>. <br /> <br /> Like, sure, <i>sometimes</i> he manages to kill the people he makes deals with before they can change their minds, but it\u2019s an inherently bad business model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T01:14:12-07:00","id":1386023,"title":"","content":"Oddly, the classic short story THE DEVIL AND TOM WALKER was a subversion of that according to the author.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Devil_and_Tom_Walker\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5b/Devil_and_Tom_Walker.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Devil_and_Tom_Walker\" target=\"_blank\"> The Devil and Tom Walker - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Devil_and_Tom_Walker\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Devil_and_Tom_Walker </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Tom meets the Devil and the Devil offers him wealth for his soul. Tom refuses.<br /> <br /> Tom's wife, a particularly awful woman, seeks out the Devil and is murdered in the woods because she's already damned.<br /> <br /> Tom then changes his mind and negotiates for his soul. The Devil tries to get him to be a slaver but he refuses and settles instead on being a banker. These are signs that Tom is not irredeemably evil but still subject to temptation and weakness. I.e. a soul who could go either way.<br /> <br /> In the end, he's only carried off by the Devil when he makes a joke about the Devil having him if he's making a cent on a deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T02:50:38-07:00","id":1386028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations#post1385888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tenents of the path seems to be all about serving the demons,doing whatever the demons want. It's basically slavery isnt it? The path doesn't mention what the infernalist gains in the whole deal. I completely understand why a vampire would deals in demons fpr money,power ir artifacts<br /> But why would anyone sell their soul if there isn't anything but slavery to receive in return?</div> </div> </div> </div>the Path is outsourcing controlling the Beast to a demon, it is the ultimate surrender of self, but unlike wassail, you keep an illusion of free will, (so basically wassail but with beer, and parties) in exchange for giving up actual will, after that, well Investments, Gifts, Dark Thaumaturgy, Discplines, material rewards etc, all can follow, but it is a master training his pet, and giving it the ability to serve better, their is a reason in Dark Ages the other Paths of the Road of Sin hate the Path of Screams (PoER in an earlier form) so much, almost more than the Paths of Heaven do. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T03:41:24-07:00","id":1386033,"title":"","content":"Get the investiture of chains and you'll not need to worry about the beast ever again, of course, presumably an investestiture is an investment and the demon doesn't just wanna give those out willy nilly. <br /> <br /> The path of revelations is just honourable accord to one guy who's a total bastard. The best and worst path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T07:13:21-07:00","id":1386059,"title":"","content":"How does that quote go? Better to rule in Hell than serve in Heaven?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T07:28:49-07:00","id":1386063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1386059#post1386059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that quote go? Better to rule in Hell than serve in Heaven?</div> </div> </div> </div>no, Revelations is more: we're going to hell anyway, so might as well enjoy ourselves","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:05:51-07:00","id":1386107,"title":"","content":"Its like Jazz. If you have to ask then you'll never know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T00:13:44-07:00","id":1386294,"title":"","content":"Revelations is a &quot;good deal&quot; even without getting any investments. Hell, even without getting a demonic master.<br /> <br /> Path of Evil Revelations (or its better version, DAV20 Path of Screams) is about replacing your moral compass with &quot;the devil made me do it&quot;. It's abdication of responsibility. You don't need to feel guilty about accidentally draining a human dry - Satan made you do it. Theft? Satan! Murder? Satan! It doesn't matter what you do - you can't <i>really</i> be judged for it because it's the demons who are <i>really</i> responsible. You aren't to blame to here! You are a good guy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:50:09-07:00","id":1386321,"title":"","content":"Personally, I much prefer the ROAD OF THE DEVIL from DA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:59:28-07:00","id":1386326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1386321#post1386321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I much prefer the ROAD OF THE DEVIL from DA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Roads are always better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T00:54:03-07:00","id":1386635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1386059#post1386059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that quote go? Better to rule in Hell than serve in Heaven?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how you view demons, it may be less of a horrible deal than it seems.<br /> <br /> The Akuma in Exalted are treated with great riches, pleasure, and wealth.<br /> <br /> They aren't abused because they want their minions to be happy when they're kicking the asses of mortals and enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T11:15:52-07:00","id":1386740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1385975#post1385975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every vampire loses their free will to some extant.<br /> <br /> The Beast has such a pervasive influence, especially as Humanity drops, that it must be terrifying to think one might become a slavering, primitive wight, barely capable of speech let alone free will. It looks a little like how in zombie movies there's always that one character who begs the others to &quot;not let me become one of those things.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Path of Evil Revelations promises not just temporal rewards (Investments, Dark Thaumaturgy, etc.), but also a means to easily avoid entering Wassail. Sure, there are other paths that don't involve slavery, but those are really hard. I mean, like getting a degree in philosophy hard. They take time, effort, study, and self-knowledge. It doesn't always work, even after all that effort.<br /> <br /> If you can find a demon, though, you just do what they tell you to do. All the time. Everytime. Usually they don't even ask anything too hard. After all, you're doing their bidding, so they'd rather if you succeed.<br /> <br /> Finally. Finally! You can relax, kick back, and let somebody else worry about all the messy moral quandries. Imagine what a relief this must be for a vampire who has been white-knuckling their control of the Beast for the past decade or century or so.<br /> <br /> Oh, somewhere down the line there'll be hell to pay... literally... but that should be centuries from now. Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is generally my view as well. All Paths of Enlightenment exist to provide something the vampire can believe in and adhere to, in place of utter thralldom to the Beast and its thoughtless indulgence. (Even Paths that value indulgence do so deliberately; unlike the Beast, which cares only for immediate gratification of any and all urges, regardless of utility).<br /> <br /> With Evil Revelations, the vampire substitutes the will of the Beast with that of &quot;the Master&quot; (the demon(s)). They don't need to worry about the moral, existential, or even practical implications of their actions. They just have to do what they're told.<br /> <br /> Paradoxically, there is liberation in submission, in the abdication of responsibility. Despite being a slave to demons, now and forever, the vampire is free from making those hard decisions. Just do what the Master says. Simple. Sublime. Enticing.<br /> <br /> Plenty of mortals do it in completely mundane scenarios. It's why Fascism gets so much traction. Some fascists want to lead, others want a leader to follow. (And if they get a chance to be the strong arm of their leader, enforcing their leader's laws, all the better).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure that I've seen some block of text in a WoD book pointing out there's a difference between someone who's almost certain to go to Hell in general and someone whose soul is pledged as the property of a specific demon. Only the latter benefits said specific demon directly, so they have good reasons for striking up bargains; it's the person pledging their soul who will ultimately be no better off than they would have been otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found exactly this relevant passage, in V20: Rites of the Blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20 Rites of the Blood, p. 117</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Vampiric Souls</span><br /> <br /> In order to forge a foedus with a demon, an individual must possess a soul, sentience, and free will. This leads to another issue: do vampires have souls? Although no one knows the true disposition of a vampire's soul, it has been proven that vampires can perform summoning rituals, they can bargain with demons, and they can make pacts involving the sale of their soul. Demons, it seems, are willing to take the risk.<br /> <br /> If a vampire is already damned by her nature as a member of the undead, how can she bargain with something she doesn't control? In reality, <b>there's a difference between a soul being damned, and a soul being claimed by a demon. A demon is interested in harvesting as many souls as possible in order to empower itself, even - perhaps especially - if those souls were headed to Hell anyway.</b><br /> <br /> The way a demon sees it, the only thing better than a cookie is a cookie you steal from someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T11:43:06-07:00","id":1386749,"title":"","content":"RE: Blunting the Beast's influence by taking a Master:<br /> <br /> A while back, I got inspired by the manga/anime Hellsing to consider a Path that mixes the ethos of the Road of Kings (in the form of the Path of Honorable Accord) and the Road of the Beast. I'd call it the <i>Path of the Hound</i>.<br /> <br /> A follower of the Path of the Hound would choose (or, as the case may be, have chosen for them by circumstance) a Master, an individual (or rarely a small group) that the vampires pledges herself to fully. It would work not unlike how I and others think Evil Revelations work: the Beast is resisted by placing the onus of moral responsibility on the Master. It's just that instead of a demon, its whatever being(s) the vampires is serving. (These can include other vampires, mages who bind the vampire with magic, or simply mortals the vampire respects).<br /> <br /> With the caveat being that the Path of the Hound requires a kind of give-and-take. The Master is expected to provide. Provide direction. Provide reward. Provide emotional engagement, though the exact nature of their interpersonal relationship can take a number of different forms, from the nurturing to the stern to the sadistic. The Master cannot simply demand obedience and have no other interactions with their Hound. Indeed, the use of the word &quot;Hound&quot; is deliberate: the vampire is this other individual's dog, and dogs are social creatures, requiring their Master's attention.<br /> <br /> One of the requirements of the Path is to always test one's bonds. Not break them deliberately, but test them. To push back. To demand attention and discipline. Part of the ethics of the Hound is to constantly strive to make the Master be more of a Master. No vampire willingly becomes the slave of another being without getting something, even if the rewards are intangible or emotional. Some vampires adopt the Path of the Hound because they're blood bound, choosing the unlife of a dog to resolve the tension between their own desires and that of their beloved master. Since the Blood Bond is based on love (usually), the thralls WANTS emotional validation from the Master.<br /> <br /> Even those not Bound who adopt the Path want their subservience to be validated, and for their Master to be the best Master they can be. Authoritative. Strong. Worthy. Able to keep the Hound's reckless Beast in check. Otherwise, what good is the Master?<br /> <br /> All Paths are built on the assumption that the vampire is getting something meaningful from the ethical system they have adopted. For Humanity, it's to cling to mortality and the ability to interact socially with others (Humanity, in my view, is the Path of the Pro-Social). For Evil Revelations, it's demonic power, and direction in a seemingly directionless world. For the Hound, it's similarly having direction, as well as an interpersonal connection (even if its a Master-Dog relationship) and the assurance that someone will be there strong enough to control their Beast (when the vampire themself may not be able to).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T13:39:08-07:00","id":1386773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385888-i-don-t-really-understand-the-path-of-evil-revelations?p=1386749#post1386749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: Blunting the Beast's influence by taking a Master:<br /> <br /> A while back, I got inspired by the manga/anime Hellsing to consider a Path that mixes the ethos of the Road of Kings (in the form of the Path of Honorable Accord) and the Road of the Beast. I'd call it the <i>Path of the Hound</i>.<br /> <br /> A follower of the Path of the Hound would choose (or, as the case may be, have chosen for them by circumstance) a Master, an individual (or rarely a small group) that the vampires pledges herself to fully. It would work not unlike how I and others think Evil Revelations work: the Beast is resisted by placing the onus of moral responsibility on the Master. It's just that instead of a demon, its whatever being(s) the vampires is serving. (These can include other vampires, mages who bind the vampire with magic, or simply mortals the vampire respects).<br /> <br /> With the caveat being that the Path of the Hound requires a kind of give-and-take. The Master is expected to provide. Provide direction. Provide reward. Provide emotional engagement, though the exact nature of their interpersonal relationship can take a number of different forms, from the nurturing to the stern to the sadistic. The Master cannot simply demand obedience and have no other interactions with their Hound. Indeed, the use of the word &quot;Hound&quot; is deliberate: the vampire is this other individual's dog, and dogs are social creatures, requiring their Master's attention.<br /> <br /> One of the requirements of the Path is to always test one's bonds. Not break them deliberately, but test them. To push back. To demand attention and discipline. Part of the ethics of the Hound is to constantly strive to make the Master be more of a Master. No vampire willingly becomes the slave of another being without getting something, even if the rewards are intangible or emotional. Some vampires adopt the Path of the Hound because they're blood bound, choosing the unlife of a dog to resolve the tension between their own desires and that of their beloved master. Since the Blood Bond is based on love (usually), the thralls WANTS emotional validation from the Master.<br /> <br /> Even those not Bound who adopt the Path want their subservience to be validated, and for their Master to be the best Master they can be. Authoritative. Strong. Worthy. Able to keep the Hound's reckless Beast in check. Otherwise, what good is the Master?<br /> <br /> All Paths are built on the assumption that the vampire is getting something meaningful from the ethical system they have adopted. For Humanity, it's to cling to mortality and the ability to interact socially with others (Humanity, in my view, is the Path of the Pro-Social). For Evil Revelations, it's demonic power, and direction in a seemingly directionless world. For the Hound, it's similarly having direction, as well as an interpersonal connection (even if its a Master-Dog relationship) and the assurance that someone will be there strong enough to control their Beast (when the vampire themself may not be able to).</div> </div> </div> </div>How can he be expected to be a good hound if he doesn't get a plasma screen TV with Netlix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:26:24-07:00","id":1386829,"title":"","content":"That's somewhat similar to how my main character conducts himself on the Path of Honorable Accord. He feels he's honor bound to serve certain vampires he respects as a result of their past mentorship, though they explicitly do not share his moral philosophy or religious faith. He doesn't serve them blindly, but he does work with their wellbeing/gain in mind and generally does what they ask of him if it doesn't require him to completely go against his own principles. (And when it does, he tries hard to find alternatives that will result in them being happy without having to violate his own codes.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","cus